          "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-measure-with-density": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-indefinite-integral-of-a-nonnegative-function-is-a-measure": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-dominated-convergence": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-real-exponential-function-and-e": "mathematical-premise",
          "cor-exponential-reciprocal-and-positivity": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-exponential-is-strictly-increasing": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-derivative-of-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
          "cor-mean-value-theorem": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Skinner, Advanced Quantum Field Theory, Chapter 2, “QFT in Zero Dimensions” (University of Cambridge Part III lecture notes)",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/dbs26/AQFT/chap2.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "Nima Moshayedi, Quantum Field Theory and Functional Integrals (lecture notes, arXiv:1902.08652)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1902.08652"
            }
          ]
        },
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice. Let $N\\ge1$ be finite, let $C$ be a real symmetric positive-semidefinite covariance matrix, let $\\gamma_C=N_N(0,C)$, let $U:\\mathbb R^N\\to[0,\\infty)$ be a real homogeneous quartic polynomial, and let $\\lambda\\ge0$. Define $Z(\\lambda)=\\int e^{-\\lambda U}\\,d\\gamma_C$ and $N_P(\\lambda)=\\int P e^{-\\lambda U}\\,d\\gamma_C$ for every real polynomial $P$.\n\nThen $0<Z(\\lambda)\\le1$, and $\\mu_\\lambda:=Z(\\lambda)^{-1}e^{-\\lambda U}\\gamma_C$ is a Borel probability measure. Every polynomial insertion is integrable under $\\mu_\\lambda$. For each integer $r\\ge0$,\n\n$$Z^{(r)}(\\lambda)=(-1)^r\\int U^r e^{-\\lambda U}\\,d\\gamma_C,\\qquad N_P^{(r)}(\\lambda)=(-1)^r\\int P U^r e^{-\\lambda U}\\,d\\gamma_C$$\n\nfor $\\lambda>0$, with continuous right derivatives of every finite order at $\\lambda=0$. No continuum field measure is asserted."
      },
      {
        "id": "def-qft-finite-wick-normal-powers",
        "kind": "definition",
        "title": "Finite covariance Wick normal powers",
        "deps": [
          "lem-qft-finite-gaussian-wick-moments",
          "def-axiom-of-choice"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "lem-qft-finite-gaussian-wick-moments": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Skinner, Advanced Quantum Field Theory, Chapter 2, “QFT in Zero Dimensions” (University of Cambridge Part III lecture notes)",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/dbs26/AQFT/chap2.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "Nima Moshayedi, Quantum Field Theory and Functional Integrals (lecture notes, arXiv:1902.08652)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1902.08652"
            }
          ]
        },
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice, let $Q\\sim N_N(0,C)$ be the centered finite-dimensional Gaussian vector of [[lem-qft-finite-gaussian-wick-moments]], and write $C_{jj}=\\mathbb E[Q_j^2]\\ge0$ for the variance of its $j$th coordinate. For each coordinate $j$ and integer $n\\ge0$, its **finite covariance Wick normal power** is the polynomial $:Q_j^n:_C$ defined by the formal generating identity\n\n$$\\exp\\!\\left(tQ_j-\\frac12t^2C_{jj}\\right)=\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty}:Q_j^n:_C\\,\\frac{t^n}{n!}.$$\n\nEquivalently,\n\n$$:Q_j^n:_C=n!\\sum_{s=0}^{\\lfloor n/2\\rfloor}\\frac{(-C_{jj}/2)^sQ_j^{n-2s}}{s!(n-2s)!},\\qquad :Q_j^4:_C=Q_j^4-6C_{jj}Q_j^2+3C_{jj}^2.$$\n\nThis is a finite-dimensional polynomial definition; it does not define a product of unsmeared continuum fields."
      },
      {
        "id": "thm-qft-finite-asymptotic-wick-expansion",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Finite interacting asymptotic Wick expansion with remainder",
        "deps": [
          "def-qft-finite-euclidean-interacting-measure",
          "thm-qft-finite-euclidean-polynomial-measure",
          "lem-qft-finite-gaussian-wick-moments",
          "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "cor-taylor-lagrange-and-cauchy-remainders",
          "thm-derivative-of-exponential",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
          "def-real-exponential-function-and-e",
          "cor-exponential-reciprocal-and-positivity"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-qft-finite-euclidean-interacting-measure": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-qft-finite-euclidean-polynomial-measure": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-finite-gaussian-wick-moments": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-axiom-of-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "cor-taylor-lagrange-and-cauchy-remainders": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-derivative-of-exponential": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-real-exponential-function-and-e": "mathematical-premise",
          "cor-exponential-reciprocal-and-positivity": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "library": "mathematics",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Skinner, Advanced Quantum Field Theory, Chapter 2, “QFT in Zero Dimensions” (University of Cambridge Part III lecture notes)",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/dbs26/AQFT/chap2.pdf"
            },
            {
              "title": "Nima Moshayedi, Quantum Field Theory and Functional Integrals (lecture notes, arXiv:1902.08652)",
              "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1902.08652"
            }
          ]
        },
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the hypotheses and notation of [[def-qft-finite-euclidean-interacting-measure]]. Let $P\\in\\mathbb R[q_1,\\ldots,q_N]$, $Z(\\lambda)=\\mathbb E_{\\gamma_C}[e^{-\\lambda U}]$, $N_P(\\lambda)=\\mathbb E_{\\gamma_C}[P e^{-\\lambda U}]$, and $\\langle P\\rangle_\\lambda=N_P(\\lambda)/Z(\\lambda)$. For every $M\\ge0$,\n\n$$Z(\\lambda)=\\sum_{j=0}^M z_j\\lambda^j+R_{M,1}(\\lambda),\\qquad z_j=\\frac{(-1)^j}{j!}\\mathbb E_{\\gamma_C}[U^j],\\qquad |R_{M,1}(\\lambda)|\\le\\frac{\\lambda^{M+1}}{(M+1)!}\\mathbb E_{\\gamma_C}[U^{M+1}]$$\n\nfor $\\lambda\\ge0$. Likewise,\n\n$$N_P(\\lambda)=\\sum_{j=0}^M a_j(P)\\lambda^j+R_{M,P}(\\lambda),\\qquad a_j(P)=\\frac{(-1)^j}{j!}\\mathbb E_{\\gamma_C}[PU^j],\\qquad |R_{M,P}(\\lambda)|\\le\\frac{\\lambda^{M+1}}{(M+1)!}\\mathbb E_{\\gamma_C}[|P|U^{M+1}].$$\n\nDefine $b_0(P)=a_0(P)$ and, for $m\\ge1$, $b_m(P)=a_m(P)-\\sum_{j=1}^m z_jb_{m-j}(P)$. Then\n\n$$\\langle P\\rangle_\\lambda=\\sum_{j=0}^M b_j(P)\\lambda^j+O(\\lambda^{M+1})\\quad\\text{as }\\lambda\\downarrow0.$$\n\nEvery coefficient is computed from finitely many Gaussian polynomial moments and hence from finitely many covariance pairings by [[lem-qft-finite-gaussian-wick-moments]]. These estimates hold separately for each finite $M$; they do not assert convergence of the infinite formal series or any continuum limit."
      }
    ]
  },
